{{also|Singleton}}
==English==
{{wp}}

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|single|-ton}}, probably following the model of {{m|en|simpleton}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɪŋ.ɡ(ə)l.tən/|a=GA,RP}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Wodencafe-singleton.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|playing cards}} A [[playing card]] that is the only one of its [[suit]] in a [[hand]], especially at [[bridge]].
# {{lb|en|playing cards}} A hand containing only one card of a certain suit.
# A [[single]] [[object]], especially one of a [[group]].
# {{lb|en|computing}} A [[class]] that may not be [[instantiate]]d more than once, i.e. that [[implement]]s the [[singleton pattern|singleton design pattern]].
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} A [[set]] with exactly one [[element]].
# A child or animal that is born singly, not as a [[twin]] or other multiple [[birth]].
#: {{ux|en|'''singleton''' preterm birth}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2015-10-23|title=Periconception Maternal Folate Status and Human Embryonic Cerebellum Growth Trajectories: The Rotterdam Predict Study|journal=PLOS ONE|url=http://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0141089|doi=10.1371/journal.pone.0141089|passage=Viable non-malformed '''singleton''' pregnancies were selected for cerebellar measurements; transcerebellar diameter, (TCD), left and right cerebellar diameters (LCD, RCD).}}
# A person without a [[romantic]] partner.
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Lessons in love|journal=w:The Sunday People|url=https://www.pressreader.com/uk/sunday-people/20220814/284094915279630|date=2022-08-14|passage=Millennials and Gen Zedders’ approach to romance can teach later-life '''singletons''' a thing or two about new relationships, according to dating agent Anna Williamson.}}
# A person without a [[dissociative identity disorder|dissociative identity]].
# {{lb|en|phonetics}} A [[single]] [[consonant]], as opposed to a [[geminated]] consonant.
#: {{ux|en|'''singleton''' sonorants}}
# {{lb|en|backgammon}} {{syn of|en|blot}}
# {{lb|en|education}} A class offered only once within a school year.

